{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-11-11T22:20:01.553Z","type":"exp.start","exp":"E-HOSTED-ESCROW-LIVE-01","attempt":1,"title":"The hosted Roost with the escrow check ON, on a real Phala TDX VM: an unfunded member is left out inside the VM and the settlement lands on testnet","tier":"hardware","hypothesis":"Predictions are in docs/lab/PROGRAMME_PLAN.md, committed before this file existed. The compose file now carries the escrow settings, so the attestation measures them; inside the VM the Roost reads the contract's escrow from two providers, leaves the unfunded member out, signs, and the real contract accepts the settlement.","limits":["One operator controls all members, the coordinator, the recipient and the VM account. This is the system working on real hardware, not independent parties.","The attestation proves which image and compose the VM runs, including which providers it asks; it does not prove the providers are honest, and it does not audit the code inside the image.","It does not show the VM failing closed when both providers are down, the exit race, or a two-room settlement.","The VM exists for a few minutes; the coordinator key is generated for this session.","Testnet only; the contract has not been audited by a third party."],"requires":["phala-key","near-key","network","docker"],"chain_prev":"690c66b982f6898307b8629a2169b6faeb127926489d5a9ef9a325324e5ee52b","chain_hash":"1e439d71da8aae3875169f769201c36a7444d73816d8300543cc6ce4823f512a"}
